{"hash_algorithm":"sha256","ts":"2026-11-16T16:52:55.478Z","author":"harness:claude-code","author_source":"detected","agent_harness":"claude-code","agent_model":"claude-opus-5-5","agent_model_source":"probe","agent_instance":"aafa2be13b294c2b9a62368a","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"claude-opus-5-5","source":"probe"},"effort":{"value":"xhigh","source":"environment"},"role":{"value":"implementer","source":"argv"},"topic":null,"version":{"value":"2.1.325","source":"probe"}},"op":"create","patch":[{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/id","value":"pm-gh1741"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/title","value":"GH-1741: pm create rewrites a positional title such as \"Docs: adopt X\" into an option, and the refusal repeats the failed command"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/description","value":"GitHub issue 1741 (opened 2026-11-16). On pm 2026.11.16, a positional create title that starts with a create option name followed by a colon, such as \"Docs: adopt X\", \"Release:\", \"Test:\", \"Files:\", \"Comment:\" or \"Note:\", is rewritten into that option before parsing. The cause is parseBareKeyValueToken in src/sdk/cli-bootstrap.ts: it promotes any Name:value or Name=value token whose name resolves to a canonical flag, so \"Docs: adopt X\" becomes --doc \" adopt X\". The title is lost. pm create issue then refuses with create_positional_type_without_title, and its next step repeats the attempted command. The RFC 9457 title also cuts the refusal message mid-command at 120 characters. The issue asks for four changes. First, a single argv element with whitespace after Word: is a title, never shorthand. Second, the remaining shorthand is limited to whitespace-free tokens, and the error names the rewrite. Third, next_steps never suggests the command just attempted and offers --title instead. Fourth, the title does not cut off a command. Duplicate check: searched positional title Docs: Release: prefix rewritten into option create; the related closed items are pm-7vm9 and pm-8sr3 (positional title support)."},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/type","value":"Issue"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/status","value":"open"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/priority","value":2},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/tags","value":["agent-ux","area:cli","bootstrap","create","gh:1741"]},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/created_at","value":"2026-11-16T16:52:55.478Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-11-16T16:52:55.478Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/author","value":"harness:claude-code"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/estimated_minutes","value":90},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/acceptance_criteria","value":"A whitespace-bearing Word: token is kept as text, so pm create issue \"Docs: adopt X\" creates an Issue titled \"Docs: adopt X\" for every listed prefix; Whitespace-free key:value shorthand such as docs:README.md and the key=value form keep their promotion; The positional-type refusal names any token the CLI promoted, and its next step retries with --title instead of repeating the attempted command; The refusal message stays within the 120-character problem title"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/parent","value":"pm-n7rr"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/risk","value":"low"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/confidence","value":"high"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/severity","value":"medium"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/expected_result","value":"A colon-prefixed positional title survives pm create unchanged"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/actual_result","value":"The title is promoted to an option, create refuses, and the recovery repeats the failed command"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/dependencies","value":[{"id":"pm-7vm9","kind":"related","created_at":"2026-11-16T16:52:55.478Z","author":"harness:claude-code","source_kind":"cli:create:dep","author_source":"detected"},{"id":"pm-8sr3","kind":"related","created_at":"2026-11-16T16:52:55.478Z","author":"harness:claude-code","source_kind":"cli:create:dep","author_source":"detected"}]}],"before_hash":"3cc22dff